 ### Regulatory angle
 
-The Consultant's Dilemma is that a local ground gateway may be technically attractive but unavailable because of national restrictions, data-residency rules or licensing.
-A regenerative gNB knows the user's identity, PLMN and verified location, so Lynq applies routing policy onboard and sends each flow through an authorised ISL/feeder path only to a policy-compliant gateway with local user-plane breakout.
-Under MNO partnerships, the MNO keeps lawful intercept on its own core.
